 ## Overview
-This method replaces procedural noise evaluation with precomputed 3D volume textures containing analytical cloud density and Signed Distance Fields (SDF) derived from tileable 3D Worley cells [S1, unofficial]. It solves the performance bottleneck of real-time procedural cloud rendering by baking physical density and local Ambient Occlusion (AO) into a 3D texture, allowing raymarchers to sample data directly [S2, unofficial]. Unlike its siblings that rely on multi-octave 2D heightmaps or procedural turbulence, this approach uses horizontal tiling and full advection support for efficient space skipping [S1, unofficial].
